---
config: tests/legacy_compatibility.config
---

Recursive type passed to an alias while constructing its declaration
typename Box(a::Any) = [|Stop | More:a|]; typename Rec = Box(Rec); Stop : Rec
stdout : Stop : Rec
args : --fresco

Let polymorphism [1]
sig pair : forall a.(a) -> (a,a) fun pair(x) { (x, x) } (pair('a'), pair(13))
stdout : (('a', 'a'), (13, 13)) : ((Char, Char), (Int, Int))
args : --fresco

Let polymorphism [2]
{sig pair : forall a.(a) -> (a,a) fun pair(x) { (x, x) } (pair('a'), pair(13))}
stdout : (('a', 'a'), (13, 13)) : ((Char, Char), (Int, Int))
args : --fresco

Monomorphic lambda bindings
(fun (p) { (p('a'), p(13))})(fun (x) { (x,x) })
stderr : @.*Type error: Type does not match the required type \(consistency\).*In expression: p\.\s*$
exit : 1
args : --fresco

A monomorphic recursive signature rejects incompatible recursive calls
sig f : modal [Wild] ((%a) -> Int) fun f(x) { ignore(f("a")); ignore(f(1)); 1}
stderr : @.*Type error: Type does not match the required type \(consistency\).*In expression: f\.\s*$
exit : 1
args : --fresco

Polymorphic recursion with signatures
sig f : forall a. modal [Wild] ((a) -> Int) fun f(x) { ignore(f("a")); ignore(f(1)); 1 } f
stdout : @fun : forall a\.modal \[effect_[0-9]+\$Wild\] \(\(a\) -> Int\)$
args : --fresco --set=show_quantifiers=true

Invalid "polymorphic recursion"
sig f : forall a. modal [Wild] ((a) -> Int) fun f(x) { var _ = x == 1; var _ = f("a"); var _ = f(1); 1 }
stderr : @.*Type error: Type does not match the required type \(consistency\).*In expression: x == 1\.\s*$
exit : 1
args : --fresco

